{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1SA",
  "chapter": 8,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, when Samuel was old, that he made his sons judges over Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the name of his first-born was Joel; and the name of his second, Abiah: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " judges in Beer-sheba.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his sons walked not in his ways, but turned aside after lucre, and took bribes, and perverted judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then all the elders of Israel assembled, and came to Samuel to Ramah,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said to him, Behold, thou art old, and thy sons walk not in thy ways: now make us a king to judge us like all the nations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the thing displeased Samuel, when they said, Give us a king to judge us: and Samuel prayed to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to Samuel, Hearken to the voice of the people in all that they say to thee: for they have not rejected thee, but they have rejected me, that I should not reign over them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "According to all the works which they have done since the day that I brought them out of Egypt even to this day, by which they have forsaken me, and served other gods, so do they also to thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore hearken to their voice: yet protest solemnly to them, and show them the manner of the king that will reign over them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Samuel told all the words of the LORD to the people that asked of him a king.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, This will be the manner of the king that shall reign over you: He will take your sons, and appoint ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for himself, for his chariots, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his horsemen; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will run before his chariots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will appoint him captains over thousands, and captains over fifties; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will set them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to till his ground, and to reap his harvest, and to make his instruments of war, and instruments of his chariots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will take your daughters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " confectioneries, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cooks, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bakers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will take your fields, and your vineyards, and your olive-yards, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the best ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and give ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to his servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will take the tenth of your seed, and of your vineyards, and give to his officers, and to his servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will take your men-servants, and your maid-servants, and your most choice young men, and your asses, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to his work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He will take the tenth of your sheep: and ye will be his servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ye shall cry out in that day because of your king which ye shall have chosen for yourselves; and the LORD will not hear you in that day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, the people refused to obey the voice of Samuel; and they said, No; but we will have a king over us;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That we also may be like all the nations; and that our king may judge us, and go out before us, and fight our battles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Samuel heard all the words of the people, and he rehearsed them in the ears of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.8.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.8.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to Samuel, Hearken to their voice, and make them a king. And Samuel said to the men of Israel, Go ye every man to his city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
